	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Onyxia's Lair is a great cavern beneath the {link:wyrmbog}Wyrmbog{/link}, in the far south of {link:dustwallow-marsh}Dustwallow Marsh{/link}. A wide tunnel slopes down from the scorched stone of the bog into the dark, and at its end opens a vast chamber of black rock, split by cracks of fire. This is the den of {link:onyxia}Onyxia{/link}, daughter of {link:deathwing}Deathwing{/link} and brood mother of the black dragonflight. Her eggs lie in the caves along its walls, and her guards stand watch in the tunnel. Few who are not of her flight have ever seen the lair and returned.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records when {link:onyxia}Onyxia{/link} first made her den in the marsh, nor how long the cavern was hers before mortals learned of it. What is known is that her brood came up out of the south and fell upon the ogres of the {red:stonemaul-ogres}Stonemaul clan{/red}. The ogres lost their village and fled north into the reeds. {link:draz-zilb}Draz'Zilb{/link}, the scholar of the Stonemaul, traced the whelps back to their mother by the arts of the arcane. He did not believe that a daughter of {link:deathwing}Deathwing{/link} had come so far only to lay siege to a band of ogres. Why she chose this marsh, so near to {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link} and to the lands of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, no one has yet learned.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:wyrmbog}The Wyrmbog{/link} has become a breeding ground. {link:onyxia}Onyxia{/link}'s eggs are scattered across the Dragonmurk, and her whelps and drakes hunt the southern marsh. In a den nearby, the ancient drake {link:emberstrife}Emberstrife{/link} tests the dragonspawn who would rise to guard her. Only the strongest of the black flight may enter her lair. They must carry a key, an amulet attuned by {red:general-drakkisath}General Drakkisath{/red} in {red:blackrock-spire}Blackrock Spire{/red}. Without it, her wards bar the way.

Some who are not dragons have found other roads to that key. The blue dragon {link:haleh}Haleh{/link} of {link:winterspring}Winterspring{/link} knows how such an amulet is made whole, and {link:rexxar}Rexxar{/link} knows how one may be won by guile and by blood. It is said that the brood mother rests in the deepest chamber of her cavern. Those who would face her must go down to her.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Within the Lair",
			text = [=[• {b}The Tunnel.{/b} A long passage winds down from the bog. Onyxian warders, dragonspawn of her guard, stand along it and let no stranger pass.
• {b}The Nests.{/b} Deep caves open off the walls of the great chamber, and their floors are covered with eggs. When their mother calls, the whelps pour out of them in swarms.
• {b}The Great Chamber.{/b} A vast hall of black stone at the end of the tunnel, where {link:onyxia}Onyxia{/link} waits. Cracks in its floor split open and spew fire. When she takes to the air, the whole cavern burns beneath her breath.]=],
		},
	},
})

